{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792333533,"nonce":"68XfXkQZ7ssk1hSfECMiKqC8NSQ=","title":"Bench: rayzor's seven Benchmarks Game kernels are not in the CI sweep","message":"rayzor benches fannkuchredux, spectralnorm, pidigits, fasta, knucleotide, regexredux and revcomp (rayzor compiler/benchmarks/haxe, BM*Code.hx); our CI sweep carried fib, binary_trees, deltablue, mandelbrot, nbody and the four call kernels. Where ash trails rayzor on those seven was measured only by hand on one machine.\n\nAdded the seven sources unchanged, their bytecode, a manifest entry each, a CI matrix leg each, titles for the site and a line of page copy. Each is judged on one printed value, read by marker: fannkuchredux \"Pfannkuchen(10) = \" 38; spectralnorm \"x1e9 = \" 1274224152; pidigits \"checksum \" 882142 last 9216420198; fasta \"hash \" 3666008; knucleotide \"GG \" 19463; regexredux the agg[act]taaa|ttta[agt]cct count 58; revcomp \"hash \" 11578911.\n\nChecked: all seven print the same on ash interp, hybrid and jit (and hybrid --no-fma), and Haxe's own evaluator prints the same values; ash_bench.py judges all seven OK in hybrid-auto; haxe compiles each to -hl C and --jvm for the rival lanes. The interpreter needs 13 to 48 s on fannkuchredux, fasta, pidigits and spectralnorm under load, so those four skip interp as nbody does.\n\nNot yet seen: a CI run (HL/C, JVM and hl2-ir lanes on the runner, and the 4-core timings).","files":null}]}